{"name":"Bulma Hair","hex":"#359e6b","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hair","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pigmented filament of keratin which grows from a follicle on the skin of humans and other mammals.","The collection or mass of such growths growing from the skin of humans and animals, and forming a covering for any part or the whole body."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the hair from.","To grow hair (where there was a bald spot)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hair"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bulma","blocks":[{"text":"Bulma  is a fictional character in the Dragon Ball franchise, first appearing in the original manga series created by Akira Toriyama, Goku's first friend and the eventual wife of Vegeta and mother of Trunks and Bulla. She made her appearance in the first chapter \"Bulma and Son Goku\", published in Weekly Shōnen Jump magazine on 19 June 1984, issue 51, meeting Goku and befriending him and traveling together to find the wish-granting Dragon Balls."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8f/BulmaToriyama.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bulma","wikidata":"Q1614785"},{"title":"Hair","blocks":[{"text":"Hair is a protein filament that grows from follicles found in the dermis. Hair is one of the distinguishing characteristics of mammals.\nThe human body, apart from areas of glabrous skin, is covered in follicles which produce thick terminal and fine vellus hair. Most common interest in hair is focused on hair growth, hair types, and hair care, but hair is also an important biomaterial primarily composed of protein, notably alpha-keratin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Gray945.png/330px-Gray945.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hair","wikidata":"Q28472"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/A_Modern_Journey_to_the_West7.jpg/330px-A_Modern_Journey_to_the_West7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/df/A_Modern_Journey_to_the_West7.jpg/330px-A_Modern_Journey_to_the_West7.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The relationship between Bulma and Goku is analogous to Wu Cheng'en's depiction of the dynamic between Sun Wukong and Tang Sanzang.[4]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AA_Modern_Journey_to_the_West7.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/Bulma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9a/Bulma.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"A teenaged Bulma as depicted in the character's first appearance.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABulma.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Bulma_%26_Trunks_cosplayers_%2812165047486%29.jpg/500px-Bulma_%26_Trunks_cosplayers_%2812165047486%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Bulma_%26_Trunks_cosplayers_%2812165047486%29.jpg/1280px-Bulma_%26_Trunks_cosplayers_%2812165047486%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Bulma_%26_Trunks_cosplayers_%2812165047486%29.jpg/500px-Bulma_%26_Trunks_cosplayers_%2812165047486%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cosplay of an older Bulma as the mother of Trunks","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABulma_%26_Trunks_cosplayers_(12165047486).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/common